WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
- Well, speaking of family,
Bryce shared this old photo,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.440
so we're gonna put that, look, okay.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.670
Where are you there?

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.160
- [Bryce] You know, I don't
even really know necessarily.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.559
- But you're winking at us.

00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:10.392
- Oh, am I?

00:00:10.392 --> 00:00:11.592
Oh, no, I'm, you know what it is.

00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:13.590
I'm very sensitive to sun.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.423
- Me too.
- Yes.

00:00:14.423 --> 00:00:16.980
So it's very likely that I
just couldn't see anything.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:17.813
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:17.813 --> 00:00:22.170
- But my family, we
always go on road trips.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.030
That's always the thing that I would do,

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.188
kind of like growing up.

00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:26.021
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:26.021 --> 00:00:27.122
- And it would always be these road trips.

00:00:27.122 --> 00:00:31.413
And no one enjoyed them
except for my mother.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:34.484
- Forced family fun.
- Yeah.

00:00:34.484 --> 00:00:35.580
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:37.590
And it was like the second
that the car door was shut,

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:39.180
we knew that there was no escaping

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:40.590
for at least six and a half hours.

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.170
And so it was just like, did
you bring the bananas with you?

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.370
Like, it was like very intense.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.880
But it was, you know, like there were,

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.580
there were definitely a
lot of great memories.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.500
And then there were a few weird ones.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.640
One time my parents were
driving from LA to Yosemite

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.860
and they left my 11-year-old brother

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.800
in a Krispy Kreme in Los Angeles.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.220
And it took them four
hours to figure it out.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.080
And they arrived in Yosemite.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.903
- [Kelly] Four hours?

00:01:08.903 --> 00:01:10.470
- That's bad, that's bad.
- Four hours, yeah.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.081
- What kind of therapy
has this one been through?

00:01:13.081 --> 00:01:14.400
- I know, I know.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.360
Well, actually--
- I feel really good

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.316
as a mother now.

00:01:16.316 --> 00:01:17.847
- I know.

00:01:17.847 --> 00:01:20.310
- It's very "Home Alone" actually.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.720
- It's totally "Home Alone."

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.807
- Um no, that was reasonable.

00:01:23.807 --> 00:01:25.436
That was, no, what?

00:01:25.436 --> 00:01:27.390
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.428
No, four hours?

00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:29.959
- Four hours.

00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:31.710
- He was at a Krispy Kreme,
it's a nice place to hang.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.760
- Yeah, there could be worst places.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.970
- Eight hours because my
parents needed to drive back

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:36.803
to get him.

00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:38.790
And my mom cried the entire time.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.810
And they show up

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.720
and my, you know, this is
a little stereotypical,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.310
so I apologize if I offend anyone.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:45.360
He was surrounded by cops

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.107
and they were all eating donuts together.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:47.940
It was fine.
(audience laughing)

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.773
- Is what it is.

00:01:48.773 --> 00:01:49.606
- [Bryce] He was fine.

00:01:49.606 --> 00:01:52.056
- I mean, we all eat donuts,
not just cops, they're good.

00:01:52.056 --> 00:01:52.889
- Yes, yes.
- They're good.

00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:54.060
- Especially when you get
there and they're warm,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:55.010
I mean, I've heard.

